# The Iron Whale - Bow - the fifth island of the library's plan The Frozen Horizon (storyline SL12, chapter 5: Boarding the Whale)
# The front half of a huge icebreaker, the Iron Whale, broken in two and thrown up on a pressure ridge of the pack: her
# rust-red hull (radio tower rooms tinted rust, three long rooms on the lower deck, the mess and galley above, the open
# foredeck with the mast), her prow on the ice. The water plant and the cargo office on the lower deck, the cargo hatch
# down to her flooded engine decks (the next island); the crew mess with its vending machine and a safe, the galley; a
# zipline from the mast's crow's nest to the crane out on the ice. Quest "Boarding the Whale" (14 steps): the ramp, the
# crew roster, the water tank's plans, the zipline to the crane, the water pipe's plans, the captain's log, the electric
# purifier's plans (galley), the mess safe (keypad; the code is in the log), the large storage's plans (cargo office:
# its bolt is out, but ice seals the hatch), DEEP 10-24: the Crane Ridge, the crane's cab, the hook's lever (it breaks the
# hatch's ice and uncovers it), the cargo hatch (the plan's done-when).
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe iron_whale_bow) through the editor's own operations. Points (metres over the
# sea): the ridge at 4 m (x -14..20, z -3..12); the ramp up its south face from 1 m at -4.5 -30; the lower deck's floor at
# 4 m, its three rooms x -6..0, 0..6, 6..12 (z 0..9; the door at -4.5 0); the upper deck at 7 m (the mess x -6..0, the
# galley x 0..6, the open foredeck x 6..12 with the mast at 10 4.5); the crow's nest at 12 m; the crane at 34 -8.
include lib_features
include lib_sea
include lib_rt
include lib_ni34
include lib_frozen
include lib_areas
# RESIZE 10-24: Radius 50 -> 90 (Height 5 -> 6), the island grows round the old content, which stays where it was.
new
gen Trees=0 Bushes=0.05 Rocks=0.3 Harvest=0.05 BeachThings=0.2
gen Seed=12501 Radius=90 Height=6 Roughness=0.4 Peaks=2 Shape=1 Style=1 BeachWidth=0.3 Cliffs=0.3 PeakShape=0.5
gen Water=0.5 SeaRocks=0.3 SeaFinds=0.3 Sunken=0.3 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0 SeaLife=0.3
generate

# --- DEEP 10-24 (one-hour pass): the ice round the bow. The Crane Ridge south-west of the ship (20 m) with the old dock
# crane on it and its ladder tower to the cab (5 ladders, top 32 m): the cab's lever drops the crane's hook through the
# ice crust that seals the cargo hatch. The whalers' ice cave south-east, the whalers' ruin south, the Whale's lifeboat
# sunk 12 m down in the west, a hummock ridge north-east. Built before the ship so the ship, the ramp and the
# discoveries sit on the final ground.
