# --- DEEP 10-24: the crane, the hook, the cave, the ruin, the lifeboat ---
story hookdrop|The crane's hook|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|You dropped the dock crane's hook through the ice crust on the cargo hatch.
place TP_SnowDrift02 hatchice at 3 6 h=4.06 sit scale=0.6
prop hatchice obj.name=hatchice
prop hatchice tint.color=#e8f0f4
prop hatchice tint.amount=0.4
prop cranelever obj.name=cranelever
prop cranelever beh.use=Pull the hook's lever
prop cranelever if.use=!signal|hookdrop
prop cranelever on.use=sound||event:/exploring/obstacles/door_explosion\nmessage||The brake lets go. The hook swings out over the bow, drops - and the ice on the cargo hatch shatters.\nsignal||hookdrop\ngive||story:hookdrop*1\nhide|hatchice\nshow|hatchzone
prop cranelever else.use=message||The hook is down. The cargo hatch is clear.
note cabchest Crane cab locker | The crane driver's locker: a thermos, his tools, a pay packet.
loot cabchest MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;TradeToken*2
prop cabchest loot.refill=0
place Note_Paper cabnote at -34.7 -21.5 h=32.2 drop yaw=150
note cabnote Crane driver's last shift | CRANE LOG - A. MOEN, DRIVER\n\nLast shift. The old dock crane was here before the Whale and will be here after her, sat on its ridge like a heron. Eleven winters I have driven it, and I never once thought I would be the last man aboard who could.\nThe stern went in the night. The crew came forward over the ice, all but the captain. She stayed aft with the boilers and the hand key and would not come. Lunde says she is stubborn. Lunde says that about the weather.\nThe cargo hatch is iced shut. The hook goes where you point it; the lever's brake is stiff, lean on it. I am too old for the ladder twice in one wind.\nSomebody go down the hatch to the stern and fetch her up. She is down there with the engines, still tapping.
note whaletally Whalers' tally | WHALERS' TALLY (cut in the cave wall)\n\nNine seasons. Forty-one whales. Old Gunnar cut a mark for every whale and a cross for every man we lost, and there are only two crosses, which is a better tally than any crew on this coast.\nThe Iron Whale took the bay in the tenth season. She broke the ice for good and the whales went with the ice. Her captain - Brask, a woman, polite as a bishop - paid us for the pots we could no longer use. We drank most of it.\nWe left the pots here in the cave. Our lifeboat - her lifeboat, she gave it us - went down off the west ice in the first storm. Its locker had the good knives. Somebody braver than us can dive for them.
note whalecavechest Whalers' pots | The whalers' pots, rimed with old fat: hooks, a harpoon head, rope.
loot whalecavechest Rope*3;Scrap*2;Leather*2
prop whalecavechest loot.refill=0
note whalelist Whalers' winter list | WINTER LIST - SIGRUN, THE WHALERS' COOK\n\nPots to the cave. Boat to the west ice, if it floats, which it will not.\nFish salted: twenty barrels. Lamp oil: four. Patience: none.\nThe old crane on the ridge still works. Its hook goes where you point it - the Whale's men used it to knock the frost off her hatches, and paid us in coffee to drive it. Good coffee, too, until the courier stopped bringing any.\nThe men say the Whale will break in spring. I say she will break when she likes, like all ships and all husbands.\nWe go south to Steamvent when the lead opens. Nobody follows the whalers. Nobody ever did.
note whaleruinchest Whalers' chest | Under the fallen wall: a lamp, a knife, some salt fish.
loot whaleruinchest Raw_GenericMeat*2;Nail*8;Glass*2
prop whaleruinchest loot.refill=0
note lifeboatchest Lifeboat locker | The lifeboat's locker, twelve metres down: flares, knives, the mate's tin.
loot lifeboatchest MetalIngot*2;CopperIngot*2;TitaniumOre*1

# --- Settings, notes, behaviours, quest -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# the generator's rocks that floated over the slope (ground check, 2026-10-23)
