info title=The Iron Whale - Bow
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The front half of a huge icebreaker thrown up on a pressure ridge: a rust-red hull to walk through, a crew mess with a vending machine and a safe, a zipline from the mast to the crane on the ice, and a cargo hatch down to her flooded stern. The fifth island of The Frozen Horizon.
island on.arrive=message||A ship's bow on a ridge of ice, rust-red, as tall as a house - the Iron Whale. Her stern is gone.

story messcode|The mess safe's code|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|You typed the captain's code into the mess safe's keypad.

note roster Iron Whale: crew roster | ICEBREAKER IRON WHALE - CREW ROSTER\n\nCaptain: H. Brask\nMate: J. Lunde\nRadio: Y. Sund\nEngineers: 4 (aft)\nCook: P. Skarre\nDeck: 9\n\nPosted by the mate, day 1 of the ice. The ridge has us by the nose and will not let go, so here is the rule: all hands sleep aft, by the boilers, where it is warm and where she will float if she breaks. The bow is for work and for meals.\nNobody walks out on the ice alone. Nobody touches the radio but Officer Sund, and she will thank you not to.\nThe cook says his name has two Rs and no E. The cook may write his own roster. - J. Lunde
note waterplant Water plant | Water plant locker: the water tank's plans, fittings, a frozen gauge.
note cranebox Crane box | The crane driver's box: the water pipe's plans and a spanner.
note captainslog1 Captain's log, day 1 | CAPTAIN'S LOG - IRON WHALE\n\nDay 1 of the ice. The pack closed round us in the night and the ridge lifted the bow clear of the water, like a hand lifting a cup. She will break, I think, aft of the funnel. I have sent the crew aft anyway; the boilers are the only warm thing for a hundred miles.\nThe Coldhold's charts and the crew's pay are in the mess safe. I set its lock to the day I took her: the fourth of the twelfth month, in the seventh year. Lunde says that is a terrible code. Lunde is right, and I am keeping it.\nThe vault wants its charts back, and it wants our radio quiet. It may have the first. I have not decided about the second.\nAll hands aft. - H. Brask
note galley Galley locker | The cook's locker by the kettle: the electric purifier's plans.
note messsafe Mess safe | The crew's pay in tokens, the Coldhold's charts in oilcloth.
note orrinpost Post for H. Brask | POST - FOR CAPTAIN H. BRASK, IRON WHALE\n\nCaptain,\nTwo letters from the Steamvent folk, a tin of tobacco for your mate, and a sealed one from the Coldhold that I am not allowed to read, and so have read no more than twice.\nNo coffee, I am sorry. There is none left north of the vents. If you have a cup to spare when I am back through, I will not say no.\nTuva and Knut send their regards. Knut ate your mate's glove. I have told him it was a fine glove and he should be ashamed, and he is not.\nThe ice south of the ridge is rotten this year; go round by the west if you walk. I will be back on the next run - sooner, maybe, if the Warden has more letters for you. He writes a great deal for a man who wants everyone quiet.\nYours on the runners,\nOrrin Vale, courier
note skarrnote The cook's complaint | FROM THE GALLEY - P. SKARR, COOK (TWO Rs, NO E)\n\nTo whoever reads this, and to the mate in particular:\nThe roster says Skarre. There is no E. There has never been an E. My mother did not cross the whole Baltic in an open boat to give me an E.\nMenu for the week of the ice. Monday: fish. Tuesday: fish, but warm. Wednesday: the captain's cake, which is fish. On Thursday the stokers asked for something that was not fish, so I boiled their gloves. They went back to fish.\nThe purifier lives by my kettle. It is the only thing on this ship that makes the water taste of water and not of Knut the sledge dog.\nWe are not sinking. I will not cook on a sinking ship. - P. Skarr
note aerialnote Aerial lead, cut | MATE'S NOTE, DAY 31 - J. LUNDE\n\nOfficer Sund came up shouting this morning: no carrier, no hiss, nothing. I thought the ice had finally pulled the mast over. It has not. The mast stands as straight as a church.\nThe aerial lead is cut, here at the mast's foot, a hand's breadth off the deck. Not frayed, not chafed - cut, clean through the copper in one stroke, the way you split kindling. There is a nick in the deck plate under it where the blade went on.\nNo ice did this. Nobody aboard owns a blade like that; I have been through every man's kit, and the cook's, twice.\nI told the captain. She went very quiet. Then she went aft, down to the engine decks, and took the old hand key with her.
note cargooffice Cargo office | Cargo office chest: large storage plans, the manifest, the hatch's bolt.
loot waterplant Blueprint_WaterTank*1;Bolt*2;Plastic*4
prop waterplant loot.refill=0
loot cranebox Blueprint_Pipe_Water*1;Scrap*3;MetalIngot*1
prop cranebox loot.refill=0
loot galley Blueprint_ElectricPurifier*1;CircuitBoard*1;Plastic*3
prop galley loot.refill=0
loot messsafe TradeToken*6;MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2
prop messsafe loot.refill=0
loot cargooffice Blueprint_Storage_Large*1;Plank*8;Nail*12
prop cargooffice loot.refill=0

